Extend $O K$ and $O M$ to intersect $O_{1} M$ and $O_{2} K$ respectively at points $L$ and $P$ (Fig. 53). In the trapezoid $L M K P$ with bases $L M$ and $P K$, we have $\frac{\left|M O_{1}\right|}{\left|O_{1} L\right|}=\frac{|M D|}{|D K|}=$ $=\frac{\left|P O_{2}\right|}{\left|O_{2} K\right|} . \quad$ Therefore, $O_{1} O_{2}$ passes through the intersection point of the diagonals of the trapezoid - point $O$. Moreover,

