Let $y / x=t$. It is not difficult to prove that the maximum value of the function $t /(1+t)^{3}$ is achieved at $t=1 / 2$ (for example, by taking the derivative of this function) and is equal to 4/27. Thus, $S_{K L M N}=2 S_{K L M}<\frac{8}{27} S_{A B C D}$.

